# 03 — Loops & Iteration

## What is this?
Loops execute a block of statements repeatedly until a termination condition is met. C provides `for`, `while`, and `do-while` loops, along with `break` and `continue`.

## Why does C have it?
- `for`: Best when the number of iterations is known in advance.
- `while`: Best when looping depends on an indeterminate runtime condition.
- `do-while`: Guarantees that the loop body executes at least once before checking the condition.

## Syntax and Core Mechanics
```c
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    if (i == 5) continue; // Skip to next iteration
    if (i == 8) break;    // Terminate loop
}
```

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `int sum_range(int start, int end)`:
   - Returns the sum of all integers from `start` to `end` inclusive. If `start > end`, return 0.
2. `long long factorial(int n)`:
   - Returns `n!` (factorial). If `n < 0`, return 0. For `n == 0`, return 1.
3. `int count_digits(int n)`:
   - Returns the number of digits in integer `n`. Handles 0 (1 digit) and negative integers.

## Progressive Hints
- Hint 1: In `sum_range`, use a `for (int i = start; i <= end; i++)` loop and accumulate.
- Hint 2: In `factorial`, initialize `long long result = 1` and multiply up to `n`.
- Hint 3: In `count_digits`, handle `n == 0` first, take absolute value if `n < 0`, and divide by 10 in a loop.

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```c
int sum_range(int start, int end) {
    if (start > end) return 0;
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {
        sum += i;
    }
    return sum;
}

long long factorial(int n) {
    if (n < 0) return 0;
    long long res = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        res *= i;
    }
    return res;
}

int count_digits(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 1;
    if (n < 0) {
        if (n == -2147483648) return 10;
        n = -n;
    }
    int count = 0;
    while (n > 0) {
        count++;
        n /= 10;
    }
    return count;
}
```
</details>

#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("Printing even numbers up to 10:\n");
    for (int i = 2; i <= 10; i += 2) {
