# 05 — Arrays & Pointer Basics

## What is this?
An array is a contiguous block of memory holding elements of the same type. A pointer is a variable that stores the memory address of another variable. In C, array names decay into pointers to their first element when passed into functions.

## Why does C have it?
- Pointers allow direct memory manipulation, pass-by-reference mutation, and zero-overhead array traversal.
- `&x`: Address-of operator (obtains memory address of `x`).
- `*ptr`: Dereference operator (reads or writes value at memory address `ptr`).

## Syntax and Core Mechanics
```c
int val = 10;
int *ptr = &val;  // ptr holds address of val
*ptr = 20;        // val is now 20

int arr[3] = {10, 20, 30};
int *p = arr;     // points to arr[0]
*(p + 1) = 25;    // modifies arr[1] to 25
```

## What to Practice
Implement in `exercise.c`:
1. `void swap_integers(int *a, int *b)`:
   - Swaps the values pointed to by `a` and `b`.
2. `int array_sum(const int *arr, int length)`:
   - Returns the sum of all elements in array `arr` of size `length`. If `length <= 0`, return 0.
3. `int array_max(const int *arr, int length)`:
   - Returns the maximum element in array `arr`. If `length <= 0`, return 0.

## Progressive Hints
- Hint 1: In `swap_integers`, use a temporary variable `int temp = *a; *a = *b; *b = temp;`.
- Hint 2: In `array_sum`, loop `for (int i = 0; i < length; i++)` and accumulate `arr[i]`.
- Hint 3: In `array_max`, initialize `max = arr[0]` and compare each element.

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```c
void swap_integers(int *a, int *b) {
    if (a == 0 || b == 0) return;
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}

int array_sum(const int *arr, int length) {
    if (arr == 0 || length <= 0) return 0;
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {
        sum += arr[i];
    }
    return sum;
}

int array_max(const int *arr, int length) {
    if (arr == 0 || length <= 0) return 0;
    int max = arr[0];
    for (int i = 1; i < length; i++) {
        if (arr[i] > max) {
            max = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return max;
}
```
</details>

